        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <title>Lesson 8 · Student Film Festival Organizer</title>\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\" />\n  <script defer src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <header>\n      <h1>Student Film Festival Organizer</h1>\n      <p>Filter short films by vibe keywords and length. Check that the total runtime fits your screening block.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"toolbar\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Display options\">\n        <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"toggle-contrast\"> High contrast</label>\n        <label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"big-text\"> Larger text</label>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"grid\">\n      <!-- Controls and results -->\n      <main class=\"panel\" id=\"left\" aria-labelledby=\"filters-title\">\n        <h2 id=\"filters-title\">Find Films</h2>\n\n        <section class=\"controls\" aria-label=\"Filters\">\n          <div class=\"control\">\n            <label for=\"vibeInput\">Vibe keywords</label>\n            <input id=\"vibeInput\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"uplifting, quiet, surreal\">\n            <p class=\"small\">Tip: press a chip to add a keyword.</p>\n            <div id=\"vibeChips\" class=\"chips\" aria-label=\"Common vibe chips\"></div>\n            <div class=\"row\">\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"matchMode\" id=\"modeAny\" checked> Match any</label>\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"matchMode\" id=\"modeAll\"> Match all</label>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"control\">\n            <span class=\"label\">Genre</span>\n            <div id=\"genreFilters\" class=\"checks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Filter by genre\">\n              <!-- checkboxes injected -->\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"control\">\n            <span class=\"label\">Length group</span>\n            <div class=\"row\">\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"lenGroup\" value=\"any\" checked> Any</label>\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"lenGroup\" value=\"short\"> Short</label>\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"lenGroup\" value=\"medium\"> Medium</label>\n              <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"lenGroup\" value=\"long\"> Long</label>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"row small\">\n              <label>Short under <input id=\"shortMax\" type=\"number\" min=\"1\" value=\"5\"> min</label>\n              <label>Medium under or equal to <input id=\"medMax\" type=\"number\" min=\"2\" value=\"15\"> min</label>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"control\">\n            <label for=\"blockMinutes\">Block length</label>\n            <input id=\"blockMinutes\" type=\"number\" min=\"10\" step=\"5\" value=\"60\">\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"row\">\n            <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"sortAsc\"> Sort by runtime</label>\n            <button id=\"clearFilters\" class=\"secondary\">Clear filters</button>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"results\" aria-label=\"Results\">\n          <div class=\"bar\">\n            <span id=\"matchCount\">0 matches</span>\n            <span id=\"totalMinutes\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">0 min</span>\n            <span id=\"passFail\" class=\"pill\">Check</span>\n          </div>\n\n          <div id=\"suggestions\" class=\"note small\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n\n          <div id=\"cards\" class=\"cards\" aria-label=\"Film cards\">\n            <!-- cards injected -->\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      </main>\n\n      <!-- Quick reference and test bench -->\n      <aside class=\"panel\" id=\"right\">\n        <h2>Quick Sum Check</h2>\n        <p class=\"muted\">The bar above shows total minutes for the current matches. It must fit your block.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>Test bench</h3>\n        <p class=\"small\">Run a check and compare to your expected minutes.</p>\n\n        <div class=\"test\">\n          <label for=\"testVibes\">Vibes</label>\n          <input id=\"testVibes\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"quiet, warm\">\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"test row\">\n          <label class=\"inline\">Group\n            <select id=\"testGroup\">\n              <option value=\"any\">Any</option>\n              <option value=\"short\">Short</option>\n              <option value=\"medium\">Medium</option>\n              <option value=\"long\">Long</option>\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <label class=\"inline\">Block\n            <input id=\"testBlock\" type=\"number\" min=\"10\" step=\"5\" value=\"60\">\n          </label>\n          <label class=\"inline\">Expected\n            <input id=\"testExpected\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\" value=\"0\">\n          </label>\n          <button id=\"runTest\">Run test</button>\n        </div>\n        <p id=\"testResult\" class=\"note small\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n\n        <hr>\n        <p class=\"small\">Need the activity steps and prompt patterns? Open <strong>Activity Progression.md</strong>.</p>\n      </aside>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": ":root{\n  --bg:#f6f7fb;\n  --ink:#111;\n  --muted:#67707c;\n  --panel:#fff;\n  --accent:#4b6bfb;\n  --border:#e5e7eb;\n  --focus:#111;\n}\n\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\n\nbody{\n  margin:0;\n  color:var(--ink);\n  background:var(--bg);\n  font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,Noto Sans,sans-serif;\n  line-height:1.5;\n}\n\n.wrap{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:1rem}\nheader h1{margin:0.25rem 0;font-size:1.4rem}\nheader p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:0.95rem}\n\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 340px;gap:1rem;margin-top:1rem}\n@media (max-width:960px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}\n\n.panel{\n  background:var(--panel);\n  border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:12px;\n  padding:1rem;\n  box-shadow:0 0.25rem 0.6rem rgba(0,0,0,0.04);\n}\n.panel h2{margin:0 0 0.5rem}\n.muted{color:var(--muted)}\n.small{font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n\n.toolbar{\n  display:flex;gap:0.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0.25rem 0 0.75rem\n}\nlabel.inline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.35rem;margin-right:0.5rem}\n\n.controls{display:grid;gap:0.8rem}\n.controls .control{display:grid;gap:0.35rem}\n.controls .row{display:flex;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}\n\ninput,select{\n  width:100%;\n  padding:0.5rem 0.6rem;\n  border:1px solid #cfd3da;\n  border-radius:8px;\n  background:#fff;color:var(--ink);font:inherit\n}\nbutton{\n  appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;\n  padding:0.55rem 0.8rem;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer\n}\nbutton.secondary{background:#e9ecf7;color:#1c2a62}\nbutton:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus);outline-offset:2px}\n\n.chips{display:flex;gap:0.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.chip{\n  padding:0.2rem 0.55rem;border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:999px;background:#fff;font-size:0.85rem;cursor:pointer\n}\n.chip.active{background:#eef2ff;border-color:#cdd5ff}\n\n.bar{\n  display:flex;gap:0.75rem;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;\n  border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:0.5rem 0.7rem;margin-top:0.6rem;background:#fff\n}\n.pill{padding:0.15rem 0.5rem;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#1d2a7a;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem}\n\n.note{\n  margin-top:0.6rem;padding:0.6rem 0.7rem;border-radius:8px;background:#fff7ed;border:1px solid #fde6c7;color:#7a4a07\n}\n.note.pass{background:#f0fdf4;border-color:#bbf7d0;color:#14532d}\n\n.cards{\n  margin-top:0.6rem;\n  display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:0.75rem\n}\n.card{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;background:#fff;padding:0.8rem}\n.card h4{margin:0 0 0.25rem}\n.meta{display:flex;gap:0.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.meta .tag{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:999px;padding:0.05rem 0.45rem}\n\n.test{display:grid;gap:0.3rem;margin:0.4rem 0}\n.test.row{display:flex;gap:0.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}\n\n.high-contrast{\n  --bg:#fff;--ink:#000;--panel:#fff;--accent:#000;--border:#000;--focus:#000\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "// Helpers\nconst $ = sel => document.querySelector(sel);\nconst $$ = sel => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(sel));\n\n// Dataset\nconst films = [\n  { title:\"Paper Planes\",       minutes:4,  genre:\"animation\",     vibes:[\"uplifting\",\"quiet\",\"hand-drawn\",\"friendship\"] },\n  { title:\"Streetlight\",        minutes:7,  genre:\"documentary\",   vibes:[\"gritty\",\"reflective\",\"urban\"] },\n  { title:\"Loop\",               minutes:12, genre:\"experimental\",  vibes:[\"hypnotic\",\"abstract\",\"sound-driven\"] },\n  { title:\"Lunch Line\",         minutes:5,  genre:\"comedy\",        vibes:[\"light\",\"snappy\",\"school\"] },\n  { title:\"Tidepool\",           minutes:9,  genre:\"documentary\",   vibes:[\"calm\",\"nature\",\"awe\"] },\n  { title:\"Pencil Test\",        minutes:3,  genre:\"animation\",     vibes:[\"playful\",\"meta\",\"weird\"] },\n  { title:\"Echo Park\",          minutes:14, genre:\"narrative\",     vibes:[\"moody\",\"slice-of-life\",\"hopeful\"] },\n  { title:\"Orbit\",              minutes:16, genre:\"narrative\",     vibes:[\"mystery\",\"tense\",\"space\"] },\n  { title:\"Spiral Stair\",       minutes:6,  genre:\"experimental\",  vibes:[\"black-and-white\",\"quiet\",\"surreal\"] },\n  { title:\"Kindling\",           minutes:8,  genre:\"documentary\",   vibes:[\"family\",\"warm\",\"rural\"] },\n  { title:\"Static Bloom\",       minutes:18, genre:\"experimental\",  vibes:[\"glitch\",\"intense\",\"loud\"] },\n  { title:\"Bus Stop\",           minutes:4,  genre:\"animation\",     vibes:[\"quiet\",\"kind\",\"minimal\"] },\n  { title:\"Salt\",               minutes:10, genre:\"comedy\",        vibes:[\"awkward\",\"dry-humor\",\"friendship\"] },\n  { title:\"Glasshouse\",         minutes:13, genre:\"narrative\",     vibes:[\"tense\",\"contained\",\"dialogue-heavy\"] },\n  { title:\"Night Swim\",         minutes:5,  genre:\"experimental\",  vibes:[\"moody\",\"water\",\"blue\"] },\n  { title:\"Sunroom\",            minutes:7,  genre:\"animation\",     vibes:[\"soft\",\"warm\",\"no-dialogue\"] },\n  { title:\"Threads\",            minutes:11, genre:\"documentary\",   vibes:[\"craft\",\"slow-burn\",\"care\"] },\n  { title:\"Open Mic\",           minutes:8,  genre:\"comedy\",        vibes:[\"crowd\",\"nerves\",\"feel-good\"] }\n];\n\n// Build chips and genre checkboxes\nconst allVibes = [...new Set(films.flatMap(f => f.vibes))].sort();\nconst allGenres = [...new Set(films.map(f => f.genre))].sort();\n\nfunction renderChips(){\n  $(\"#vibeChips\").innerHTML = allVibes.map(v => `<button class=\"chip\" data-v=\"${v}\" aria-pressed=\"false\">${v}</button>`).join(\"\");\n}\nfunction renderGenreChecks(){\n  $(\"#genreFilters\").innerHTML = allGenres.map(g => `\n    <label class=\"inline\"><input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"${g}\" checked> ${g}</label>\n  `).join(\"\");\n}\n\n// Group logic\nfunction groupFor(mins, shortMax, medMax){\n  if (mins < shortMax) return \"short\";\n  if (mins <= medMax) return \"medium\";\n  return \"long\";\n}\n\n// Filtering\nfunction currentFilters(){\n  const vibeText = ($(\"#vibeInput\").value || \"\").toLowerCase();\n  const vibeTokens = vibeText.split(/[, ]+/).map(t => t.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  const matchAll = $(\"#modeAll\").checked;\n  const selectedGenres = $$(\"#genreFilters input[type=checkbox]\")\n    .filter(cb => cb.checked).map(cb => cb.value);\n  const lenGroup = document.querySelector(\"input[name=lenGroup]:checked\").value;\n  const shortMax = parseInt($(\"#shortMax\").value, 10);\n  const medMax = parseInt($(\"#medMax\").value, 10);\n  const block = parseInt($(\"#blockMinutes\").value, 10);\n  const sortAsc = $(\"#sortAsc\").checked;\n\n  return { vibeTokens, matchAll, selectedGenres, lenGroup, shortMax, medMax, block, sortAsc };\n}\n\nfunction matchesFilm(f, filters){\n  const { vibeTokens, matchAll, selectedGenres, lenGroup, shortMax, medMax } = filters;\n\n  // Genre filter\n  if (selectedGenres.length && !selectedGenres.includes(f.genre)) return false;\n\n  // Vibes\n  if (vibeTokens.length){\n    const lcVibes = f.vibes.map(v => v.toLowerCase());\n    const hasToken = t => lcVibes.some(v => v.includes(t));\n    if (matchAll && !vibeTokens.every(hasToken)) return false;\n    if (!matchAll && !vibeTokens.some(hasToken)) return false;\n  }\n\n  // Length group\n  const g = groupFor(f.minutes, shortMax, medMax);\n  if (lenGroup !== \"any\" && g !== lenGroup) return false;\n\n  return true;\n}\n\nfunction filterFilms(){\n  const filters = currentFilters();\n  let list = films.filter(f => matchesFilm(f, filters));\n  if (filters.sortAsc){\n    list.sort((a,b) => a.minutes - b.minutes || a.title.localeCompare(b.title));\n  }\n  return list;\n}\n\n// Rendering\nfunction renderResults(){\n  const list = filterFilms();\n  const block = parseInt($(\"#blockMinutes\").value, 10);\n  const total = list.reduce((s,f) => s + f.minutes, 0);\n  const pass = total <= block;\n\n  $(\"#matchCount\").textContent = `${list.length} matches`;\n  $(\"#totalMinutes\").textContent = `${total} min`;\n  $(\"#passFail\").textContent = pass ? \"Fits block\" : \"Too long\";\n  $(\"#passFail\").className = pass ? \"pill\" : \"pill\";\n  const suggestion = suggest(list, block, total);\n  const sugEl = $(\"#suggestions\");\n  if (list.length === 0){\n    sugEl.className = \"note\";\n    sugEl.textContent = \"No matches. Try fewer vibe keywords or switch to Match any.\";\n  } else if (pass){\n    sugEl.className = \"note pass\";\n    sugEl.textContent = \"Good to go. Your picks fit the block.\";\n  } else {\n    sugEl.className = \"note\";\n    sugEl.textContent = suggestion;\n  }\n\n  $(\"#cards\").innerHTML = list.map(f => `\n    <article class=\"card\" aria-labelledby=\"t-${slug(f.title)}\">\n      <h4 id=\"t-${slug(f.title)}\">${f.title}</h4>\n      <div class=\"meta\">\n        <span class=\"tag\">${f.genre}</span>\n        <span class=\"tag\">${f.minutes} min</span>\n        <span class=\"tag\">${groupFor(f.minutes, parseInt($(\"#shortMax\").value,10), parseInt($(\"#medMax\").value,10))}</span>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"small\">${f.vibes.join(\", \")}</p>\n    </article>\n  `).join(\"\");\n}\n\nfunction slug(s){ return s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,\"-\"); }\n\nfunction suggest(list, block, total){\n  const over = total - block;\n  const longest = list.slice().sort((a,b)=>b.minutes-a.minutes)[0];\n  const groups = {short:0, medium:0, long:0};\n  const shortMax = parseInt($(\"#shortMax\").value,10);\n  const medMax = parseInt($(\"#medMax\").value,10);\n  list.forEach(f => groups[groupFor(f.minutes, shortMax, medMax)]++);\n  if (groups.long > 0) return `Try Short or Medium only. Removing the longest film (${longest.minutes} min) saves time. Over by ${over} min.`;\n  if (groups.medium > 0 && groups.short === 0) return `Switch to Short only. That usually fits a 60 minute block. Over by ${over} min.`;\n  return `Reduce vibe requirements or limit to one or two genres. You need to cut ${over} min.`;\n}\n\n// Event wiring\nfunction bindEvents(){\n  // Text and selects\n  [\"vibeInput\",\"shortMax\",\"medMax\",\"blockMinutes\"].forEach(id=>{\n    $(`#${id}`).addEventListener(\"input\", renderResults);\n  });\n  $$(\"#genreFilters\").forEach(()=>{\n    $(\"#genreFilters\").addEventListener(\"change\", renderResults);\n  });\n  $$(\"#modeAny,#modeAll\").forEach(el => el.addEventListener(\"change\", renderResults));\n  $$(\"input[name=lenGroup]\").forEach(el=>el.addEventListener(\"change\", renderResults));\n  $(\"#sortAsc\").addEventListener(\"change\", renderResults);\n\n  // Chips\n  $(\"#vibeChips\").addEventListener(\"click\", e=>{\n    const b = e.target.closest(\".chip\"); if(!b) return;\n    const v = b.getAttribute(\"data-v\");\n    b.classList.toggle(\"active\");\n    const tokens = new Set($(\"#vibeInput\").value.toLowerCase().split(/[, ]+/).filter(Boolean));\n    if (b.classList.contains(\"active\")) tokens.add(v);\n    else tokens.delete(v);\n    $(\"#vibeInput\").value = Array.from(tokens).join(\", \");\n    renderResults();\n  });\n\n  // Display toggles\n  $(\"#toggle-contrast\").addEventListener(\"change\", e=>{\n    document.body.classList.toggle(\"high-contrast\", e.target.checked);\n  });\n  $(\"#big-text\").addEventListener(\"change\", e=>{\n    document.body.style.fontSize = e.target.checked ? \"18px\" : \"\";\n  });\n\n  // Clear filters\n  $(\"#clearFilters\").addEventListener(\"click\", ()=>{\n    $(\"#vibeInput\").value = \"\";\n    $$(\"#genreFilters input[type=checkbox]\").forEach(cb => cb.checked = true);\n    document.querySelector(\"input[name=lenGroup][value='any']\").checked = true;\n    $(\"#shortMax\").value = 5; $(\"#medMax\").value = 15;\n    $(\"#blockMinutes\").value = 60; $(\"#sortAsc\").checked = false;\n    $$(\"#vibeChips .chip\").forEach(c=>c.classList.remove(\"active\"));\n    $(\"#modeAny\").checked = true;\n    renderResults();\n  });\n\n  // Test bench\n  $(\"#runTest\").addEventListener(\"click\", ()=>{\n    const vibes = ($(\"#testVibes\").value || \"\").toLowerCase();\n    const group = $(\"#testGroup\").value;\n    const block = parseInt($(\"#testBlock\").value, 10);\n    const expected = parseInt($(\"#testExpected\").value, 10);\n\n    // Temporarily compute with these inputs\n    const filters = currentFilters();\n    filters.vibeTokens = vibes.split(/[, ]+/).map(t=>t.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n    filters.lenGroup = group;\n    filters.block = block;\n\n    const list = films.filter(f => matchesFilm(f, filters));\n    const total = list.reduce((s,f)=>s+f.minutes,0);\n    const pass = total <= block;\n    const verdict = (total === expected) ? \"Totals match\" : `Expected ${expected} min, got ${total} min`;\n    $(\"#testResult\").className = pass ? \"note pass small\" : \"note small\";\n    $(\"#testResult\").textContent = `${verdict}. ${pass ? \"Fits the block.\" : \"Too long for the block.\"}`;\n  });\n}\n\n// Initial paint\nrenderChips();\nrenderGenreChecks();\nbindEvents();\nrenderResults();\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "progression.md",
          "language": "md",
          "contents": "# Lesson 8 · Student Film Festival Organizer\nContext: plan a one hour screening block. Search by vibes and length, check the sum, and revise.\n\n## 1) Orientation\n- Set **Block length** to 60 minutes.\n- Read the results bar. Note **match count**, **total minutes**, and **Fits block** or **Too long**.\n- Try one vibe like `quiet`. Add one more. Watch the total change.\n\n## 2) Decide length groups\nDefault: Short under 5 minutes, Medium under or equal to 15 minutes, Long above 15 minutes.  \nYou can change the numbers and test effects.\n\n- Switch **Length group** to Short. Record how many matches and minutes you see.\n- Try Medium and Long. Record the totals again.\n- Pick a group that helps your block stay within 60 minutes while keeping variety.\n\n## 3) Clarity, readability, and accessibility\nUse the toggles to evaluate the interface.\n- **High contrast** on. Check headings, borders, and chips for readable contrast.\n- **Larger text** on. Confirm no labels overlap or clip.  \n- Read the **summary bar** out loud. If it feels wordy, draft a simpler line.\n- Keyboard test. Tab to chips, then Space or Enter to toggle a chip.\n- A quick check: can a classmate find the **total minutes** in three seconds or less?\n\n**Prompt pattern**\n> Rewrite the results bar text so a ninth grader understands it in one glance. Keep the same numbers.\n\n## 4) Bias and perspective scan\nYou control what plays first. That choice shapes attention.\n- Try only one **genre**. What voices or styles go missing?\n- Sort by runtime. Do the shortest films capture the screening just because they fit?\n- Pick two vibe words that might exclude voices. Replace them with broader terms.\n- Note one film you included and one you left out. Explain the tradeoff in one sentence.\n\n**Prompt pattern**\n> Suggest a more inclusive vibe label to replace \"<term>\". Provide one reason in 12 words or fewer.\n\n## 5) Accuracy and label improvements\n- Inspect film cards. Are the labels clear and consistent with the dataset?\n- Replace any jargon in your notes with words students use.\n- If a label is ambiguous, propose two alternatives and justify the better one.\n\n**Prompt pattern**\n> Propose two clear label options for \"<current label>\" and explain which is better for students.\n\n## 6) Build features with CHAT\nYou will use this process while working in the app.\n\n### Clarify\n- State the goal, fields, and success check.\n- Example:\n  > Implement a search that filters by vibe keywords and a length group. Show total minutes above the results. Pass when total minutes are visible and update as filters change.\n\n### Hone\n- Add one improvement and keep it simple.\n- Options:\n  - Add a pass or fail pill for the block limit.\n  - Add a second search check for **genre**.\n  - Add a quick suggestion when the total is too long.\n\n**Prompt pattern**\n> Add a short suggestion when total minutes exceed the block. Use one sentence and name the longest film.\n\n### Apply\n- Ask for three example searches with expected totals.\n- Run each search in the app. Compare your total to the expected total.\n- If totals do not match, adjust the check or the filters and retest.\n\n**Starter prompt**\n> Output three example searches as vibe lists with group and expected total minutes. Keep the format compact and testable.\n\n### Transfer\n- Draft a compact template you can reuse in other projects.\n\n**Template starter**\n1) Goal: filter by keywords and a second field, then report a sum.  \n2) Inputs: items with `title`, `minutes`, `genre`, and a list of `vibes`.  \n3) Rules: plain words, short sentences, and a visible pass or fail check.  \n4) Outputs: a result bar with match count, total minutes, and a suggestion.  \n5) Self‑check: change one filter and confirm both the total and the pass or fail update.\n\n## 7) Test set\nAsk AI for three example searches with minutes to expect. Enter them in the **Test bench** and record pass or fail with one note each.\n\n## 8) Reflection\nWrite two lines:\n- One design choice that improved fairness or clarity and why it matters.\n- One film you dropped and one you kept, plus the reasoning.\n\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "1",
        "2",
        "3",
        "4"
      ]
    }
